# nwn-mdl-spec conformance probe zspec_kid5 (CC0-1.0)
# Numbering against a supermodel node that is itself numbered -1: zspec_mid's
# 'cape' is -1 (zspec_super lacks it), its children cape_a and cape_b have
# numbers. Shows whether the walk goes on through the -1 node (cape_b and
# cape_a take zspec_mid's numbers, cape_x, which zspec_mid lacks, -1 under a
# matched parent) or stops there (fresh count + 1 + declaration index).
# The children are declared in another order than in zspec_mid, so fresh
# numbers could not coincide with zspec_mid's.
newmodel zspec_kid5
setsupermodel zspec_kid5 zspec_mid
classification character
beginmodelgeom zspec_kid5
node dummy zspec_kid5
  parent NULL
endnode
node dummy hips
  parent zspec_kid5
endnode
node dummy cape
  parent zspec_kid5
endnode
node dummy cape_x
  parent cape
endnode
node dummy cape_b
  parent cape
endnode
node dummy cape_a
  parent cape
endnode
endmodelgeom zspec_kid5
donemodel zspec_kid5
